{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/audit/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T23:31:45.771953Z","id":"f7c5549039d624ec57c298a75fc04d541ed9a54baf93fadb88630adbcc4fd06e","body":{"detail":"content_manifest_sha256 now skips clax.json (clax_core::manifest::MANIFEST_PATH). versions.content_sha256 written before that, for a version whose files held a clax.json of the page's own, still counts the file. crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs put_app_bundle (around :116) compares the hash the app computes for the files (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/content_hash.dart contentHash, which also skips clax.json) to the stored one, so exporting such a version as an app bundle is refused bundle_mismatch; crates/clax-store/src/backfill.rs (around :1958) recomputes and compares stored hashes the same way. No migration rewrites them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":660},"end":{"line":683},"content_hash":"af602d4a6f8afa19f2847caa8ce760ba5637b922a499e743045303dc07a2d6ff"},"suggested_fix":"A migration that recomputes content_sha256 for versions whose files_json names clax.json, or comparisons that accept the hash with clax.json counted for versions written before the change.","summary":"A version that held a page's own clax.json before content hashes left it out keeps a stored content_sha256 a fresh computation no longer gives","tags":["clax-json","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
